//! task: write
//! ask: Write `signum`, taking an i32 and returning -1, 0 or 1, using a three-way condition.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.5
//! explain: `si … sin … aliter` is the whole conditional ladder. `sin` is classical Latin for "but if" and takes the place of `else if` / `elif`; `aliter` ("otherwise") is the final branch. Every branch ends in `redde`, so no join is needed after the ladder.

publica functio signum(x: i32) -> i32 {
    si x lt 0 {
        redde -1;
    } sin x eq 0 {
        redde 0;
    } aliter {
        redde 1;
    }
}
